mation in addition to  that I'm a Sony distinguished engineer  we've been working for with Google for  about eight years now where GC where GCP  customers  we're also G's  customers and that's how we we first  came into contact with one another we've  been talking to Google about rendering  in the cloud since before GCP was even a  product offering from Google so a really  long time at this point so image works  is a little unique within the post  production space and that it  simultaneously works on both visual  effects projects in full-length animated  features using the same production  pipeline so typically you work on one or  the other but not both and that's what  makes us unique we've been in business  for over 25 years have worked with all  the major motion picture studios on well  over a hundred projects at this point  we're headquartered in British British  Columbia in Vancouver have an office in  Culver City and run a large datacenter  in Quincy Washington at peak we grow to  about 1300 artists operate tens of  thousands of rendering cores and manage  multiple petabytes of storage so here's  a high-level picture of our wide area  network we've run multiple 10 gig  wavelength services that connect Seattle  Vancouver Quincy in Culver City we  operate our own MPLS network to provide  both redundancy and flexibility so you  can think of this as an MPLS cloud we  maintain points of presence in Vancouver  Seattle in Los Angeles and we currently  pier with Google in Seattle to reduce  the network latency back to our Quincy  data center we're also working on  establishing another peering  relationship in downtown Los Angeles  that we can take advantage of the new  Los Angeles data center all our projects  are bid and our fixed fee our workforce  tends to be ephemeral and scales up and  down and sync with the cyclical and  seasonal nature of our business by  cyclical I mean the times of year such  as the summer and the key holiday  periods in which large tentpole 